==German==
===Etymology===
{{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|sizzen}}, originally *{{term||sitten}}.  Cognate with English {{term|sit}} and Dutch {{term|zitten}}.

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{intransitive}} to [[sit]]; to [[perch]]
# {{intransitive}} to [[stay]] (in one place); to [[remain]]; to [[be]] (in a particular place or state)
# {{intransitive|of clothing}} to [[fit]]
# {{intransitive|colloquial|lang=de}} to [[do time]]; to [[spend]] time in jail
# {{intransitive|colloquial|of a strike, a comment, etc.|lang=de}} to [[hit home]]; to have a significant effect

====Conjugation====
{{de-conj-strong|sitz|saß|gesessen|h|||säß|a|a|||a}}

====Usage notes====
The standard auxiliary verb used with the past participle {{term|gesessen}} is {{term|haben}}.  In Upper German dialects (High German dialects spoken primarily in Austria, Switzerland, southern Germany, and Northern Italy), the auxiliary verb {{term|sein}} is used instead.

